(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "mangaka.layout.komawari (ai-gftd-mangaka/clj/src/mangaka/layout/komawari.cljc) is the first algorithmic generator for :panel/rect/:panel/tilt/:panel/polygon/:panel/z/:panel/bleed in mangaka.gftd.ai's domain schema" "a komawari force-line row shares ONE tilt across every panel in that row (row-tilt picks the highest-intensity beat's vector) rather than tilting panels independently, so adjoining internal gutters stay a constant-width parallel channel" "the impact tilt bound is derived from the golden ratio itself (Math/atan(1/phi) ~= 31.7 degrees), not an arbitrary degree count" "mangaka.graphs.compose-komawari (NSID ai.gftd.mangaka.composeKomawari) is a hand-built plan->govern->render->persist graph, not built on mangaka.graphs.gen (which assumes a comfy txt2img render step this graph doesn't have) -- a governor-rejected layout is never persisted" "mangaka.preview/panel-svg was extended (not replaced) to draw <polygon> when :panel/polygon is present, honoring ai-gftd-mangaka/clj/CLAUDE.md's rule against reintroducing a bespoke SVG/canvas renderer as storyboard SSoT" "kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page's layout-page now returns 3-tuples [panel rect tilt] (was 2-tuples [panel rect]); tilt is nil unless a panel opts into :intensity/:vector, so every pre-existing caller/test sees byte-identical rects" "kami-mangaka-page and ai-gftd-mangaka are independent, unrelated consumers (per ADR-2607022800 cluster 43) -- the golden-ratio + force-line-shear design was ported as duplicated pure math in both, not shared as a dependency" "ghosthacker/260123-jump/resources/episodes/ep1-komawari-redesign/episode.edn compresses manga_script.edn's 17-page Episode 1 (v3, Daimon Construction arc) into a 5-page komawari-annotated script, actually run through ai.gftd.mangaka.composeKomawari (governor ok on all 5 pages) and rendered to SVG -- this is a name (panel-layout + dialogue placement draft), not inked/illustrated art, since no image-generation tool was connected in this session")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "komawari-golden-ratio-force-line-panel-layout"), (:adr/related (vector "adr-2606282100" "adr-2607022800")), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607051520-komawari-golden-ratio-force-line-panel-layout"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-06"), (:adr/body "See the companion .md file in this same directory for the full context, decision, consequences, and alternatives (identical content, kept in sync)."), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/artifacts "{:ai-gftd-mangaka \"gftdcojp/ai-gftd-mangaka @ 885a03ef2e86f421a920511e278a38cbc49fc9ff (PR #4, merged) -- new src/mangaka/layout/komawari.cljc + src/mangaka/graphs/compose_komawari.cljc + preview.cljc polygon support; registry.cljc/langgraph.edn composeKomawari entry; test/mangaka/layout/komawari_test.cljc + core_test.cljc additions; clojure -M:dev:test 90 tests/563 assertions, 1 failure/1 error both pre-existing (comfy-stub env, unrelated to this change -- confirmed via git stash baseline re-run)\", :kami-mangaka-page \"kotoba-lang/kami-mangaka-page @ 45148cdf8858818815043b2f9df76a208d1060f0 (PR #1, merged) -- additive komawari-tilt/shear-polygon in page.clj, layout-page 3-tuple extension; clojure -M:test 9 tests/28 assertions, 0 failures (was 7/21 before, all pre-existing assertions unchanged)\", :ghosthacker-episode \"com-junkawasaki/ghosthacker @ 979a2bf32e15ffc7cb17ec346743e7767a91aa10 (PR #12, merged) -- 260123-jump/resources/episodes/ep1-komawari-redesign/episode.edn, 5-page komawari-annotated script; ai.gftd.mangaka.composeKomawari run against all 5 pages, governor :ok? true / 0 issues on every page\"}"), (:adr/date "2026-07-05"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607051520: komawari(コマ割り)設計 — 黄金比 × フォースライン panel layout"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))